WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.883
India's inflation target

2
00:00:01.883 --> 00:00:02.767
is 4 percent.

3
00:00:02.967 --> 00:00:04.882
But the RBI isn't told to

4
00:00:04.882 --> 00:00:05.954
hit exactly 4.

5
00:00:06.454 --> 00:00:07.990
The target comes with a band:

6
00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:09.995
2 to 6 percent, on retail

7
00:00:09.995 --> 00:00:10.757
inflation.

8
00:00:11.207 --> 00:00:13.587
Under the RBI Act, the government

9
00:00:13.587 --> 00:00:15.534
sets it with the RBI, every

10
00:00:15.534 --> 00:00:16.327
five years.

11
00:00:16.727 --> 00:00:18.865
In March 2026, it kept the

12
00:00:18.865 --> 00:00:20.921
target at 4 percent, plus

13
00:00:20.921 --> 00:00:21.825
or minus 2,

14
00:00:21.925 --> 00:00:23.568
until March 2031.

15
00:00:24.018 --> 00:00:25.400
Stay outside the band for

16
00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:26.727
three quarters in a row,

17
00:00:26.827 --> 00:00:28.513
and the RBI must report to

18
00:00:28.513 --> 00:00:30.135
the government: why, what

19
00:00:30.135 --> 00:00:31.691
it will do, and by when.

20
00:00:32.141 --> 00:00:34.253
It sent its first such report

21
00:00:34.253 --> 00:00:35.491
in November 2022.

22
00:00:35.941 --> 00:00:37.199
The number is the aim.

23
00:00:37.399 --> 00:00:39.490
The band is the accountability.

24
00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:40.865
Your turn.

25
00:00:41.015 --> 00:00:42.593
What is the tolerance band

26
00:00:42.593 --> 00:00:44.535
around India's inflation target?
